Issue labels can route `/iflow-pick`: `{{ yolo_label }}` → `/iflow-run yolo`, `{{ ops_label }}` → no-PR close (ops wins over yolo). A `{{ publish_label }}` label makes `/iflow-close` bump the version and release after merge.
{%- endif %}

## Branch hygiene

- Work on an issue branch `<N>-<short-slug>`, never on the default branch.
- Before continuing a branch, run `git fetch --prune` and check ahead/behind against `origin/<default>`. PRs are **{{ pr_merge_method }}**-merged, so a merged branch looks "ahead" and is stale.
{% if auto_cleanup %}- `auto_cleanup = true`: after a PR merges, run `/iflow-cleanup`.
{% elif remind_cleanup %}- After a PR merges, remind the user to run `/iflow-cleanup`. Do not run it automatically.
{% endif %}- An issue already under `{{ partly_solved_folder }}/` or `{{ solved_folder }}/` has a stale branch. Re-open it only on purpose with `/iflow-pick <N>`.

## Multi-repo workspaces

When the workspace holds several repos with their own `{{ issueflows_dir }}/`, resolve the target repo first (`root:` / `repo:` hints, then `issue-flow agent resolve`, then the `issueflow-workspace.toml` default); ask when ambiguous. Pass `--repo <owner/repo>` to every `gh` call. Lifecycle state is per repository.
